# Normalise all text files to LF in the working tree. The repo already
# stores LF; this makes that consistent on a Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true, where git would otherwise materialise CRLF and break
# tests that match source files against a literal `\n` (see #771).
* text=auto eol=lf

# No tracked file in this repo is binary today (verified against the full
# `git ls-files` list — no images, fonts, or certs; WhatsApp auth state and
# `*.pem`/`*.key` files are .gitignore'd, never tracked). If a binary asset
# is added later, give it its own `-text` (or `binary`) line here rather than
# letting `text=auto` guess.
